# Force LF for everything Biome formats, regardless of a developer's local
# core.autocrlf. Without this, Windows checkouts (autocrlf=true) round-trip
# source files to CRLF, and Biome (which defaults to LF) then reports them as
# unformatted even though nothing meaningful changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch line endings. `bun.lockb` in particular: `text=auto`'s
# heuristic can misdetect it and corrupt it byte-for-byte (caught in review —
# a renormalize shrank it from 564500 to 563300 bytes).
bun.lockb binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
